            "review_title": "Review at Bang Khuang Cafe",
            "review_text": "Van N\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam24 contributions\n0\nOldest cafe of oldest family in Buon Ma Thuot\nJan 2016 • Friends\nJust across the street from the oldest temple of the city. The cafe was etablished in 1967 and haven't changed name since then. Home grown coffee still brewed in their traditional way. The family was one fo the first family came to Buon Ma Thuot with the last king of Viet Nam. Their coffee has a distintive strong taste not by bitterness but by the condensation of coffee brewed 2 times and let sleep overnight. There are 2 different spaces. The left one owned by the youngest brother and the right one owned by eldest sister. Although both serve coffee prepared by the mother but the sister's one has much better space and service. We really enjoy having coffee here every morning of our trip.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten January 17, 2016",
